			<div class="content" id="post-content-4805725">
									

<p>First off, I adore this. As one who isn't <em>necessarily</em> keen towards any characterisations of the O5 Council, this article kept me engaged, entertained, and thoroughly invested on the actions of O5-8, O5-10, and Kristine. The length of the article did not phase me, as the events flowed and blended so smoothly that the length seems warranted.</p>
<p>Some nitpicks, for you</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This was personally ordered by the Overseer, with the reasoning behind it has been classified.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This appears fragmented. I would suggest maybe changing this to something like, &quot;This was personally ordered by the Overseer, with the reasoning behind it being strictly classified.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Next thing you know it, I'll get killed in my sleep.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The &quot;know it,&quot; seems personally a bit wonky. Maybe you could just omit &quot;it&quot; and instead keep it as &quot;Next thing you know, I'll get killed in my sleep&quot; (usually thats how its typically stated anyways)</p>
<p>Despite these nitpicks, I genuinely enjoyed this article, and I'm glad you could achieve something so phenomenal based off one photo and a rough description! :)</p>

