<p>So overall I liked this, I think the story told overrides any problems I have with it. So I’m upvoting&#8230;.</p>
<p>But:</p>
<ul>
<li>this overstays it’s welcome dramatically. I think there’s a lot of bloat that could be trimmed down, especially in the dream sequence once 05-8 is in the machine.</li>
<li>The dialogue is rough in parts, everyone curses so much&#8230; and it’s not just that they curse, O5-10 and O5-8’s log is full of really childish language. It feels like two teenagers arguing. Same could be said for O5-10’s journals. The phrasing just doesn’t fit a super powerful executive type in his forties.</li>
<li>This is probably just a me problem, but the internal logic of the way the votes occur bothers me. When the second meeting (where only 4 O5s bother to show and vote) occurs, there’s no way they’d have quorum to make a binding decision. If a board of directors had 12 members and only 1/3 of them showed, the regulations/bylaws would clearly state that any vote wouldn’t have an effect. I get that it was probably so you only had limited interactions in a dialogue, but you could add something that those who didn’t appear gave their proxies to those that did&#8230; (again this is probably just a Grigori being a lawyer thing, so feel free to ignore this point)</li>
</ul>

